INTERPRETATION
The Z3 solver ranges over unbounded integers ell,d,s,t with
ell-d=2Q, Q>=7, the alcove bounds, and the required parity.  A mask
records the parameter parities, every lower-maximum tie,
upper-minimum tie, branch activation, and possible j=1 weight
truncation in the four signed affine-fold branches.  Blocking complete
masks and exhausting the solver is an exact census, not a bounded scan.
The two joint censuses use common level, label, source, target, parity,
and fusion-wall selectors for the powers that occur in the same packet.
They are the exact common refinements needed for an individual matrix
entry.  They do not yet perform the variable-range suffix sum over the
crossing coordinate, so they are not by themselves a packet-sign
certificate.

